      "writtenOn": "2024-11-27T19:43:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a new API where the currently merged implementation (merged a few weeks ago) ensures compatibility of creating normal listener using socket settings but without any of the offload related methods guarded by the flag `bt_offload_socket_api`, such as `getDataPath()` etc.\n\nSo if the `socket_settings_api` is released but not `bt_offload_socket_api`, it will just create a normal listener without using any of the offload related settings. It will throw errors if the caller tries to create offload settings though. If `socket_settings_api` is rolled back, then it won\u0027t call the methods guarded by `bt_offload_socket_api` since the flag check at the `listenUsingSocketSettings` will fail.\n\nPlease feel free to let me know if my understanding is correct here. Thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "7e0536ba_029fc3e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4596,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 4596,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "17288e3d19652e55b3a3c41a5ff1fb5524988e28",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
